{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383430-exalted-essence-anima-powers","id":1383430,"title":"Exalted: Essence anima powers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-23T13:08:28-07:00","id":1383430,"title":"Exalted: Essence anima powers","content":"So, in Essence, anima powers work kind of differently.<br /> <br /> Everyone has an always-on effect. Then they have, IIRC (can't find the post, if anyone finds it post it), another power that comes on when they flare, and another power that comes on when they flare iconically.<br /> <br /> So... what could these be?<br /> <br /> So for example perhaps a Wood Aspect always gets a bonus against poison and disease, a Defence buff against wooden weapons when flaring, and when they're iconic they poison people nearby. Maybe a No Moon gets the ability to detect magical sites normally, a bonus (rather than penalty) to stealth when flaring, and a bonus to spellcasting and magic when flaring iconically.<br /> <br /> Or some such.<br /> <br /> So what do you think? How closely do you think they'll hew to normal 3rd edition's anima powers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T13:32:45-07:00","id":1383433,"title":"","content":"From what I have heard, for the Caste Powers they have been wanting to get it down into the 5 Solar Archetypes, Warrior, Leader, Savant, Assassin, and Diplomat.<br /> <br /> Of course not all the Castes will adhere to this, but its mainly to allow them all to all work under the same premise for Mixed-Circle games","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T04:09:25-07:00","id":1383553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383430-exalted-essence-anima-powers?p=1383433#post1383433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I have heard, for the Caste Powers they have been wanting to get it down into the 5 Solar Archetypes, Warrior, Leader, Savant, Assassin, and Diplomat.<br /> <br /> Of course not all the Castes will adhere to this, but its mainly to allow them all to all work under the same premise for Mixed-Circle games</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Opens the can of worms of what the archetypes are for other splats' castes or aspects so they are equally easy to drop into a mixed circle.<br /> <br /> For DBs, especially given Heirs, and Lunars, archetypes are something I feel 3e has done a good job of... I initially wrote getting away from but that's not right... broadening?<br /> <br /> For example, Air is still super stealthy and good at being assassins, but Water being inherently sneaky means you can achieve similar things with slightly different approaches better than ever in 3e.<br /> <br /> Would be sad to see that knocked back a peg or two, but guess simplicity/accessibility is the intended goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T04:25:48-07:00","id":1383557,"title":"","content":"Neall did talk a little about that, but I got the impression it was more about presentation and making it easy for new players to grasp, rather than a mechanical thing.*<br /> <br /> So, perhaps it'd be more about the order that the Castes are presented.<br /> <br /> So Dawn/Zenith/Twilight/Night/Eclipse, Full Moon/No Moon/Changing Moon, Mars/Venus/Jupiter/Saturn/Mercury, Fire/Earth/Air/Water/Wood, Jade/Orichalcum//Starmetal/Adamant/Moonsilver.......<br /> <br /> Nah, this really isn't working. Kind of awkward to fit them in, and the orders look really weird (people expect the planets/days of the week to be in order, etc).<br /> <br /> Maybe it's more just the presentation in each thing. Like &quot;Fire are passionate warriors,&quot; &quot;Earth are the centre of their Circle,&quot; &quot;Adamant are mysterious and stealthy spy-assassins who serve the Divine Ministers&quot;, &quot;Jupiter chooses scholars,&quot; etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T04:43:33-07:00","id":1383562,"title":"","content":"*I think sometimes in 3rd edition different Castes across different splats have different anima powers just for the sake of it.<br /> <br /> For example, Full Moons have a bonus to, say, being able to lift really heavy objects and running really fast, which fits Creation's greatest predators more than Creation's greatest warriors. Similarly the Dawn's ability to use the most complicated and difficult combat techniques more often fits them better than it does Full Moons.<br /> But both have a bonus to resetting initiative. Full Moons have a better, much more expensive initiative booster that's once/battle. Dawns' isn't as good, but it's cheaper and can be used repeatedly.<br /> If things are being simplified, why not just give them both an initiative-related bonus that's the same?<br /> <br /> <br /> On an unrelated matter, I think because the idea was to give everyone in 3rd ed 3 anima powers, quite a few Exalt types have some really important, thematic and significant anima powers, and others that are less so. Also, some represent similar things.<br /> <br /> For example, Dawns get a bonus to intimidation, a power that represents them being really skilled at combat, and another power that represents them being really skilled at combat. The second and third ones could easily be changed to something else that represents being really skilled at combat if necessary (it probably isn't, just making a point). The first one could be swapped for something else (say, a bonus to resisting Fear like Full Moons) and I don't think it'd really be an issue. Not saying it should be, just that it could.<br /> Similarly, Air Aspects get to jump well, ignore falling damage, blow away ranged projectiles, and 1/day get a bonus on a social or mental action representing a principle. Any of them could be changed in mechanical implementation, and if the bonus reflecting your principles didn't turn up, I don't think this would destroy the point of Air Aspects (not saying it's bad and should be dropped, it's not, but I mean the writers don't need to force it in if it doesn't work well due to a changed Intimacy system or the way Animas work).<br /> <br /> (Huh, I just noticed that the Wood Aspects in 3rd ed have lost their bonus against wooden weapns and instead can ignore penalties to movement rolls or Evasion. Didn't realise that, even though I'm playing a Wood Aspect.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hmmmm... I wonder how, in a system where you have 1 always-on anima power, one at flaring and one at iconic, Night Caste's powers will work? Their power to hide their identity when iconic still works of course. But &quot;don't flare&quot; or &quot;ignore penalties to Stealth&quot; might need to be reworked.<br /> <br /> I also have wondered if there's no personal and peripheral essence in Essence (it'd simplify things) and Anima works either by just how many motes you've spent, or even you can just choose to bring it up to get the bonus. Because either of those would really alter how Night's work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T07:44:17-07:00","id":1383598,"title":"","content":"Night Castes could have the limit on flaring from mote expenditure increased. Like, they gotta spend 10m at once to raise a level instead of 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"",