epresent similar things.<br /> <br /> For example, Dawns get a bonus to intimidation, a power that represents them being really skilled at combat, and another power that represents them being really skilled at combat. The second and third ones could easily be changed to something else that represents being really skilled at combat if necessary (it probably isn't, just making a point). The first one could be swapped for something else (say, a bonus to resisting Fear like Full Moons) and I don't think it'd really be an issue. Not saying it should be, just that it could.<br /> Similarly, Air Aspects get to jump well, ignore falling damage, blow away ranged projectiles, and 1/day get a bonus on a social or mental action representing a principle. Any of them could be changed in mechanical implementation, and if the bonus reflecting your principles didn't turn up, I don't think this would destroy the point of Air Aspects (not saying it's bad and should be dropped, it's not, but I mean the writers don't need to force it in if it doesn't work well due to a changed Intimacy system or the way Animas work).<br /> <br /> (Huh, I just noticed that the Wood Aspects in 3rd ed have lost their bonus against wooden weapns and instead can ignore penalties to movement rolls or Evasion. Didn't realise that, even though I'm playing a Wood Aspect.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hmmmm... I wonder how, in a system where you have 1 always-on anima power, one at flaring and one at iconic, Night Caste's powers will work? Their power to hide their identity when iconic still works of course. But &quot;don't flare&quot; or &quot;ignore penalties to Stealth&quot; might need to be reworked.<br /> <br /> I also have wondered if there's no personal and peripheral essence in Essence (it'd simplify things) and Anima works either by just how many motes you've spent, or even you can just choose to bring it up to get the bonus. Because either of those would really alter how Night's work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not trying to brag but I did a post to propose alternative Anima powers for Solars, I decided to do this after I reached the same conclusion than you that most anima powers are really replaceable or extremely specific","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T12:36:39-07:00","id":1383655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383430-exalted-essence-anima-powers?p=1383598#post1383598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Night Castes could have the limit on flaring from mote expenditure increased. Like, they gotta spend 10m at once to raise a level instead of 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be fine. But, saying that, if anima works the same as before (you can spend X motes with no flare, then after than that each 5m puts you up a level of flare) then the current &quot;spend +X motes to not flare&quot; is fine. Though your suggestion I guess is a better system.<br /> <br /> But what I wondered was if it's working in a very different manner, how could that work with Nights?<br /> <br /> Like, what if there is no personal or peripheal essence, it's all peripheral? (But maybe spending more is required to flare or something) I guess Nights could still work similarly.<br /> <br /> But what if spending motes works radically differently? Or anima is unrelated to spending motes? Like, you just decide to go up in Anima because it gives you a buff or lets you unlock your most powerful charms? Etc. But that's quite difficult to guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T12:51:45-07:00","id":1383661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383430-exalted-essence-anima-powers?p=1383632#post1383632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not trying to brag but I did a post to propose alternative Anima powers for Solars, I decided to do this after I reached the same conclusion than you that most anima powers are really replaceable or extremely specific</div> </div> </div> </div>This is sort of true.<br /> <br /> Dawns: Be scary, have good combat skill, have good skill. Zeniths: cremate corpses, force spirits to appear, combat bonuses vs demons/undead/etc. Twilights: teleport to a place of power, control spirits, be tough. Nights: hide your Solar-ness, be stealthy, hide your identity under Solarness. Eclipses: Sanctify oaths, learn spirit magic, have diplomatic protection in spirit/ghost/Fae courts.<br /> <br /> So some can be done mechanically in different ways (combat bonuses vs Creatures of Darkness, for example). Some I think are awkward with a &quot;you get 1 all the time, 1 with caste mark, 1 when flaring iconically&quot;. Some are I think not the best expression of that Caste, or something that was brought in for 3rd edition which lacks the kind of weight of something that's been around for ages in terms of its significance in Exalted... but then, that last one makes no difference to new players.<br /> <br /> Anyway. I would quite like to see a different set of Twilight anima powers (as I think the current ones are very, very sorcery-themed) but that's not really about simplifying the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T06:04:19-07:00","id":1383759,"title":"","content":"The first dawn anima power already only works at bonfire, so that one's easy enough to port.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}